Z||000000||fropuff||08-19-2000||11:11 AM||||Hey, I was just wondering how much it would cost to repaint my gray ground effects.  What happened was my paint guy told me to mask before I started sanding.  So, I just taped so it wouldn't rough up the paint on them.  Well, when we were ready to really mask it, he told me to take off the old tape.  Well, I started on a corner, pulled it at 180 degrees while spraying WD-40 in it so it wouldn't wreck the paint.  The WD-40 didn't work!  So, when I was done, some paint was off (a lot) on every panel of the ground effects.  I am going to strip down the wheels myself soon, and I was wondering how much it would cost to get the ground effects painted as well as the wheels.  I'm keeping them gray, and want the ground FX to match the wheels.  I'm not talking about a MACCO job now.  I'm talking about a pro job, like COOTER's.  How much do you think this would cost, COOTER?  I'm not taking it to the same paint guy again.  Too much work for me; WAY too many delays.  I'm still waiting to get it buffed.  I was done sanding the new paint a week and a half ago.  Jeez!  Oh, thanks.||||reg||8
Z||000001||fropuff||08-19-2000||11:31 AM||||I also forgot to ask:  How much paint would it take to do the ground FX and wheels?  It took 3.5 pints to do the whole car; maybe 1-2 pints?  Thanks.||||reg||1
